&lt;li&gt;Triage and counsel stakeholders on ad hoc legal, compliance, and operational matters as they arise, and over time build depth in the areas most relevant to Peregrine’s business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor (J.D.) degree and active admission to practice in at least one U.S. jurisdiction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in commercial/transactional legal work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with technology transactions or general commercial contracting preferred (SaaS agreements, licensing, vendor contracts, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about new areas of legal practice and a desire to broaden your skill set to operate across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound commercial judgment, and the ability to explain legal risk to non-lawyers in plain terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, low-ego, collaborative communicator and team player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: San Francisco, New York City, or Washington, D.C. Employees in this role are expected to be in the office 4 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$225,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Peregrine is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Community Engagement Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to build and lead the function responsible for how we engage the communities we serve and drive success in the civic arena.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;As Peregrine’s technology is adopted by state and local governments, decisions about deployment can play out through public hearings, council votes, community conversations, and high-visibility civic debates. This role ensures Peregrine and our government partners are prepared to navigate those moments with credibility, transparency, and trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This is a founding role with national scope and significant ownership, sitting at the intersection of government affairs, communications, public relations, and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your North Star:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Build the strategy, relationships, and playbooks that help communities understand Peregrine’s work, surface and address legitimate concerns, and build durable public support for successful deployments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Lead community engagement strategies for Peregrine deployments by mapping civic and political landscapes, identifying key stakeholders and influencers, conducting community listening, and preparing Peregrine and government partners for public meetings and high-visibility moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Build Peregrine’s community engagement playbook by creating scalable approaches for stakeholder mapping, community listening, coalition building, public meeting preparation, and responding to emerging concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Translate Peregrine’s technology into community value by partnering with Sales, Product, Marketing, and Implementation teams to explain complex technology in clear, accessible language grounded in local priorities and civic values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Shape the public narrative around Peregrine’s work by monitoring public discourse, media coverage, and stakeholder sentiment; identifying emerging concerns or misinformation; and developing clear, fact-based communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Build trusted relationships across the civic ecosystem, including community organizations, civil rights advocates, faith leaders, business and economic development groups, public safety leaders, policy influencers, and local media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Support government partners through high-stakes civic moments, including public hearings, council votes, community meetings, and other processes that can influence the success of a deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Partner cross-functionally across Peregrine to ensure community perspectives are incorporated into how we communicate, position, and deploy our technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What Success Looks Like:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Successful Peregrine deployments supported by thoughtful, credible community engagement strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;A scalable community engagement playbook that can be applied across jurisdictions nationwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Strong relationships with community leaders and civic stakeholders in Peregrine’s key markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Government partners who are better prepared to navigate public processes and community concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Clear, accessible understanding of Peregrine’s technology and its impact among the communities we serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Early identification and effective response to emerging concerns, misinformation, and public opposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;8+ years of experience navigating local or state political environments, public affairs, government relations, campaigns, or community engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Deep understanding of how civic decisions are made and how initiatives move through city halls, public hearings, and local government processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Proven ability to build coalitions, navigate high-stakes public conversations, and move complex initiatives toward successful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Strong relationships and working familiarity with community organizations, elected officials, government leaders, or other civic stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to translate complex or technical concepts into clear, compelling narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;High-agency, entrepreneurial operator who is comfortable building from scratch and working across functions in a fast-paced, mission-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Strong judgment and credibility when operating in politically sensitive or high-visibility environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Experience working with public safety, government technology, or other complex civic issues is highly valuable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Located in NY and willing to work in the office 4 days/week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Background:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You may have served as a:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chief of Staff to a mayor, council member, or elected official&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Political campaign manager or senior campaign operative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public affairs or government relations leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Policy director or senior advisor in local or state government&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Community engagement lead on high-visibility civic initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$165,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Peregrine is looking for a Compensation Lead to architect and run the programs, frameworks, and analytics that support our people through every phase of growth. This role owns compensation strategy, job architecture and leveling, compensation cycles, equity programs, and compensation analytics—and partners closely with Talent Acquisition, People, Finance, and company leadership on how we pay, level, and reward people as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a build-and-run role. You&#39;ll design the compensation philosophy, build the job architecture and leveling framework, own our merit and compensation review cycles end-to-end, and give recruiters, HRBPs, and managers the tools they need to make confident pay decisions. You&#39;ll also build the analytics muscle that surfaces market competitiveness, band positioning, and pay equity before anyone has to ask. As Peregrine grows, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to expand your scope and shape how the compensation function evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale the philosophy and framework.&lt;/strong&gt; Assess Peregrine&#39;s existing compensation programs, data, and decision-making processes, and recommend a roadmap that supports growth from roughly 500 to 1,500+ employees. Refine and document a compensation philosophy covering market competitiveness, internal equity, and the roles of base, bonus, and equity. Establish principles for market data, peer groups, and geographic positioning, and translate them into repeatable guidelines for hiring, promotions, and merit decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the job architecture.&lt;/strong&gt; Design and implement a company-wide job catalog, job families, career tracks, and leveling criteria. Reconcile the new architecture with existing departmental frameworks, and partner with functional leaders, HRBPs, and Talent Acquisition to validate and drive adoption. Establish compensation bands backed by market benchmarks and internal equity principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the compensation cycles.&lt;/strong&gt; Run Peregrine&#39;s merit and compensation review process end-to-end—including planning, modeling, guidelines, manager inputs, approvals, communications, and post-cycle analysis. Build promotion, off-cycle adjustment, and retention award processes that scale with headcount growth. Partner with Finance to model costs and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable recruiters and managers.&lt;/strong&gt; Build tools and guidance so recruiters can self-serve the compensation inputs they need to construct and close offers. Define offer-setting guidelines and manager enablement materials. Establish a clear escalation process for exceptions, and use feedback to keep programs useful and understandable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive analytics and controls.&lt;/strong&gt; Build compensation metrics and reporting that give People, Finance, and leadership visibility into market competitiveness, band positioning, and pay equity. Own survey participation and benchmarking cadence. Run recurring pay equity, comp-ratio, and offer-outcome analyses, and turn findings into recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve equity programs.&lt;/strong&gt; Build the framework for new-hire, promotion, and refresh equity grants, balancing attraction and retention against dilution and affordability. Help candidates, employees, and managers understand equity as part of total compensation through clear tools and communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support executive- and board-level compensation.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop market-informed points of view on executive compensation and prepare clear, defensible analyses for leadership and board discussions in partnership with People and Finance leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You easily move between strategic design and hands-on execution—you can architect the framework and also build the spreadsheet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an effective influencer and listener — able to bridge the world between new Peregrine systems around comp and job families, and the messy, on-the-ground reality of differing departmental contexts, dynamics, and stages of maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re adaptable and flexible, able to think about what will worst best for Peregrine from first principles, while still balancing that with best practices and uncompromising focus on results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You partner effectively with recruiters, HRBPs, executives, and board members by communicating clear, well-supported compensation recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience creating programs and infrastructure from the ground up and improving existing processes as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You assess ambiguous situations and determine when a formal program is warranted versus when a pragmatic, lighter-weight solution will work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable turning messy data into a clean analytical model and translating insights into clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Look For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive experience in compensation, with direct ownership of compensation strategy, job architecture, and program design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building compensation infrastructure through significant headcount growth, ideally in technology or other high-growth environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in equity compensation, market benchmarking, and job leveling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of HR and compensation systems and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in San Francisco and able to work in the office 4 days/week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
