&lt;li&gt;Partner with product marketing, growth marketing, and leadership to position Peregrine’s responsible AI platform and bring products, customers, and impact to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor a team of designers and agency partners, while helping the team continue to grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the full brand system, including visual identity, motion, digital, and environmental design, and maintain the supporting design resources and templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concept, design, and art-direct emotionally resonant campaigns and brand experiences across advertising, recruiting, events, and talent brand initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key brand advisor to the executive team and translate complex business goals into clear, compelling creative work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple projects end-to-end with strong prioritization, clear timelines, and cross-functional communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Look For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in art direction and brand design, with a proven track record in both top-tier creative agencies and high-growth in-house environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio of work showcasing mastery in branding, interactive web/mobile design, video, and integrated marketing for complex technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persuasive presentation and communication skills and the ability to tie creative to strategy and goals, understanding the relationship between business strategy and brand design, with the ability to translate complex concepts (like data governance and semantic ontology) into innovative branding experiences that resonate with customers and communities alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and leading high-performance creative teams in a fast-paced environment; ability to drive multiple initiatives with a strong sense of urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in San Francisco and willing to come into the office 4x/week.&lt;/li&gt;
