&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Deal Desk &amp;amp; Pricing Analyst to own how we structure, price, review, and approve complex deals – acting as the central partner to Sales, Finance, Contracts, Sales Operations, Product, and technical teams so the business can move quickly without compromising deal quality or Peregrine&#39;s financial health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage pricing and deal requests across Salesforce, email, and direct outreach – partnering with Sales from early discovery through final commercial alignment, and prioritizing urgent opportunities within agreed-upon service levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design pricing structures, review nonstandard deal terms, and route opportunities through the appropriate approval paths, acting as the hub between Sales, Finance, Contracts, Sales Operations, Product, and technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze deployment complexity, connected systems, support needs, cloud costs, discount patterns, margins, and payment terms to flag potential revenue leakage and its impact on margins, customer perception, and close rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve flexible pricing models and tools – including the pricing calculator – that help Sales structure deals accurately, profitably, and consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input into packaging and pricing approaches for large deployments, new customer types, and other nonstandard use cases, in partnership with Finance leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a deal scorecard and approval matrix defining requirements by deployment type, size, and complexity, and establish clear approval thresholds, checklists, routing rules, and templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map workflows to identify bottlenecks and drive improvements through standardized templates, automation, and Salesforce or CPQ enhancements – improving quote-to-close time, approval velocity, and Sales enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service-oriented and action-biased: you understand Deal Desk exists to help Sales close efficiently while protecting Peregrine&#39;s long-term financial health, and you&#39;re comfortable driving toward scalable solutions in ambiguity rather than waiting for a perfect process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financially and commercially sharp: you can assess deal economics – margin impact, cash flow timing, payment terms, discounts – and explain the business implications clearly to Sales and Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at pricing and deal structure: you build and maintain financial models and help Sales structure deals that are fast, accurate, profitable, and scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous: you know overlooked terms or errors can have real consequences, and you build systematic controls that prevent mistakes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator and systems thinker: you translate complex pricing and deal risk into concise, practical guidance, build credibility across cross-functional partners, and identify workflow inefficiencies worth fixing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8+ years of experience in Strategic Finance, FP&amp;amp;A, Deal Desk, or a related pricing function (Revenue Operations, Sales Strategy), with a strong foundation supporting sales teams through complex or nonstandard commercial opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, using, or improving pricing and financial models, and translating ambiguous inputs into actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, proficiency with Excel or Google Sheets, and experience working in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the financial implications of commercial terms (margin impact, payment terms, cash flow timing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a fast-moving environment with shifting priorities, applying sound business judgment to balance precision with practical decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, service-oriented approach with clear communication skills and the ability to influence stakeholders who don&#39;t report to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience pricing an all-inclusive platform or services-enabled software (vs. seat/usage/SKU-based), partnering directly with Product, improving Salesforce/CPQ configurations or deal-routing automation, or working at a larger tech company with established commercial practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
