&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical foundation:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Data Engineering, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Presence &amp;amp; Velocity:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement and commitment to be in office 4+ days per week at our [LOCATION] office, collaborating in person to push the boundaries of what our team can achieve together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and passion to travel approximately 50% of the time, often on short notice, to lead deployments on-site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Clearance: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You currently hold an active U.S. Top Secret security clearance (required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$190,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Director of Communications at Peregrine, you’ll be part of a growing Communications team responsible for telling Peregrine’s company and technology story across external and internal audiences, including media, third-party validators, customers, prospects and partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in SF and reporting to the VP of Communications, the Director of Communications will drive our integrated technology, product and AI communications program, increasing awareness of Peregrine and our platform across audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person is a critical member of our team, focused on amplifying Peregrine’s technological vision by illustrating the value we deliver across traditional and new media audiences. The ideal candidate is a hands-on communications pro with a passion for crafting compelling company and product narratives, developing thought leadership content and platforms for our executive teams and working across the organization to drive results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a critical thinker with strong writing and communication skills, deep AI/Security/public safety product knowledge, a wide network of relationships across traditional and new media, excitement to experiment and a passion for pioneering the future of cities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of our external product, technology and AI communications strategy in partnership with internal stakeholders including product and growth marketing, content, and leadership teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with an external PR agency to craft and execute our communications strategy across traditional and new media (Substack, podcasts, speaking, awards and influencers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow and diversify our thought leadership around topics of AI, trust, privacy, data governance and technology in real-world applications, including building an engineering and product blog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally on external events and brand marketing opportunities to amplify Peregrine’s leadership and support internal communications moments, including the monthly All Hands, an internal newsletter for cross-company alignment, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to be successful in this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in Communications either in-house, agency or a combination of both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have deep new and traditional media relationships, strong writing skills and a finger on the pulse of what’s making headlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All-around Communications pro across external and internal communications initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who loves working across different teams in the company to drive alignment and clarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$228,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$266,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Executive Assistant Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly organized, proactive, and experienced Executive Assistant to support our Chief Financial Officer and Chief Legal Officer. This role provides high-touch, hands-on executive support in a fast-paced, high-growth environment. The ideal candidate has prior experience supporting C-suite executives, thrives in a dynamic startup environment, and enjoys the day-to-day responsibilities of being a trusted Executive Assistant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is well suited for someone who is exceptionally organized, resourceful, and adaptable, with the ability to manage complex calendars, coordinate meetings and travel, anticipate executive needs, and navigate shifting priorities with ease. Sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to stay several steps ahead are essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serving as a key administrative partner to both executives, you will help keep their days running smoothly, ensure their time is managed effectively, and coordinate the details that allow them to stay focused on their respective responsibilities. You&#39;ll be comfortable operating with a high degree of autonomy, handling confidential information, and bringing structure and organization to an evolving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide comprehensive administrative support to the CFO and CLO, including complex calendar management, scheduling, meeting coordination, and inbox support as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate domestic and international travel arrangements, expense reports, and other administrative logistics for both executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage competing priorities, anticipate scheduling conflicts, and exercise sound judgment when managing requests and protecting executive time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate leadership meetings, team events, offsites, and other internal and external engagements, ensuring all logistics and materials are organized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the coordination and preparation of business reviews, quarterly meetings, and board materials, including gathering content, organizing presentations, and following up with relevant stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with meeting preparation and coordination related to company and departmental OKRs, ensuring materials, schedules, and logistics are in place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a point of contact for internal and external stakeholders, helping manage requests, coordinate communication, and ensure appropriate follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of executive needs, identify potential issues before they arise, and help both executives navigate a fast-moving and ever-changing schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the CFO and CLO’s direct reports and cross-functional teams to drive alignment, operational efficiency, and process improvements across the Finance and Legal organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build empathetic relationships with ease, maintaining strong situational awareness of team culture and morale while helping executives recognize key milestones and achievements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We Look For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience directly supporting C-suite executives, ideally within a startup or high-growth company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multiple executives simultaneously, with the ability to balance competing priorities and manage complex schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong traditional EA skill set, including calendar management, travel coordination, expense reporting, meeting planning, and general administrative support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly proactive and anticipatory, with the ability to think ahead, identify potential challenges, and independently manage day-to-day executive needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment with shifting priorities and ambiguity; able to adapt quickly and bring structure to evolving situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of discretion, sound judgment, and professionalism when handling confidential information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoys providing hands-on executive support and takes pride in being an exceptional Executive Assistant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in person four days per week in our San Francisco office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$135,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Peregrine builds software that helps public safety agencies make faster, smarter decisions with their data. Our platform brings together complex data systems, empowering organizations to do their best work. We’re growing quickly and expanding into new industries and geographies. To support that growth, we’re looking for a Leadership Researcher / Sourcer: a researcher at heart who happens to source. You’ll map markets from scratch, segment them intelligently, and use that research to identify and engage exceptional executive and senior leadership talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Research is the core of this role. For each search, you’ll build the market view first: which companies matter, how their leadership is organized, and where the strongest talent sits. Then you’ll engage the people you’ve uncovered. You’ll partner closely with recruiting leadership, hiring executives, and senior leadership to bring exceptional leaders into Peregrine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead research and market mapping for each search, building a comprehensive view of the relevant leadership talent landscape, from scratch where none exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Segment markets by stage, scale, business model, growth trajectory, and organizational maturity to build target-company ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map leadership teams and org structures within target companies to identify who owns the relevant scope, as well as high-potential leaders one level below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify non-obvious and adjacent talent pools rather than relying solely on obvious competitors, titles, or previously known candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate research into actionable market insights (talent availability, org structures, candidate patterns) for recruiters and hiring executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with recruiting leadership and hiring executives to turn leadership hiring needs into clear search strategies and candidate profiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively source and engage passive leadership candidates through thoughtful, highly personalized outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct intake conversations that assess leadership trajectory, scope, impact, and motivations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organized, up-to-date pipelines and candidate activity in our applicant tracking system and recruiting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high bar for candidate experience and discretion, particularly on confidential or highly sensitive searches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we look for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of research and sourcing experience for senior or executive-level talent, in executive search or in-house at a fast-paced, high-growth company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building research from the ground up: market maps you created, not just maintained.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mapping multiple distinct markets and understanding growth-stage companies, including how stage and scale shape leadership structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong market-segmentation instincts, whether refined in an executive search firm or in-house.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to research organizational structures and identify the actual scope and reporting lines of executives (not simply searching by title).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and creativity in how you uncover talent beyond traditional channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to connect authentically with senior leaders and represent Peregrine’s mission, team, and culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in applicant tracking systems and recruiting tools to manage pipelines and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and discretion with confidential searches and sensitive organizational information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$164,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$192,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
