&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Peregrine is building a modern, AI‑native growth engine to support our next phase of scale across segments, geographies, and GTM motions. As Performance Marketing Lead, you will build Peregrine’s performance marketing function from the ground up, owning everything from foundational tracking and measurement to campaign execution, experimentation, and optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a true &lt;strong&gt;zero‑to‑one builder role&lt;/strong&gt;. While some paid programs exist today, there is no mature system in place. You will design and implement the full performance marketing operating model: defining conversion events, standing up dashboards, launching and scaling channels, and establishing how paid media drives awareness, pipeline, and expansion across complex B2B and B2G customer journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate with significant autonomy and accountability, partnering closely with product marketing, demand generation, field marketing, GTM operations, and analytics, but ultimately owning growth outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers a rare opportunity to build the performance marketing studio for a unicorn company from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own Peregrine’s central performance marketing function from the ground up, establishing the systems, playbooks, workflows, and operating rhythms that power customer acquisition and expansion as part of the Digital Marketing Studio build-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own performance marketing strategy and execution end-to-end, including budget allocation, forecasting, prioritization across segments and markets, and accountability for engagement, pipeline, and ROI targets. &lt;strong&gt;This is a hands-on role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to ad copy, creative (in collaboration with our in-house Design team), and landing page creation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument and manage the full performance marketing measurement stack, including conversion events, attribution logic, dashboards, reporting, experimentation (incrementally and lift testing), and full-funnel performance metrics used to guide investment decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, launch, and optimize global paid programs across search, paid social, programmatic, CTV, ABM, and emerging formats, managing performance from awareness through expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the in-house expert on performance channels, partnering with product marketing, field marketing, GTM operations, and growth marketing to support segment-level revenue goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deploy AI-native systems to accelerate creative development, increase testing velocity, improve personalization, and automate performance analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to SEO/AEO/GEO strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience owning performance marketing execution across paid search and paid social, with exposure to CTV, display, programmatic, ABM, and emerging formats, ideally in a B2B/B2G context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build performance marketing systems where none existed; comfort operating with ambiguity and imperfect data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in channel evaluation and optimization, including building cross‑channel dashboards and performance management workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands‑on experience designing and executing incrementality or causal measurement frameworks (e.g., lift tests, geo‑tests, structured experimentation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with DSPs, OOH formats, and managing ad inventory to support regional surge campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven use of AI‑native workflows to evolve performance marketing execution (e.g., creative iteration, testing velocity, personalization, automation, insight generation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of MAPs, CRMs, and modern BI / analytics tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or at an AI‑native or highly technical ad agency is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SEO/AEO/GEO concepts and experience using paid media and traffic insights to contribute to keyword and content strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset - you’re constantly driving toward better ways to get to outcomes, not just turning dials to tweak point metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 Days:&lt;/strong&gt; Core tracking, dashboards, and conversion events are live; initial paid programs are relaunched with clear hypotheses and success criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 Months:&lt;/strong&gt; A repeatable experimentation and optimization cadence is established, with early evidence of incremental pipeline impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within 12 months:&lt;/strong&gt; Peregrine has a scalable, data‑driven performance marketing engine with clear playbooks, predictable contribution to pipeline, and a roadmap for continued expansion, supporting diverse objectives across awareness and direct-response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might thrive in this role if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love data and measurement, and go deep to understand what’s working, what’s not, and why&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are already AI‑native, and have meaningfully re‑architected parts of your ads workflow to move faster, test more, and automate intelligently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are obsessive about details, from event definitions to experiment design to data quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy trying new channels and formats, and know how to design disciplined experiments that lead to scalable learnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are highly independent, results‑oriented, and energized by owning outcomes end‑to‑end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excited to build (not just run) a performance marketing system for a category‑defining company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$145,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Recruiting Coordinator to join our Recruiting Operations team. Reporting into the Talent Operations Lead, you will be a critical player on the recruiting team to support coordination for all roles across the company. You will be essential in managing recruiting coordination activities and creating a positive candidate experience for both virtual and in-person interviews. You will provide candidates with their first impression of Peregrine when they come onsite, delivering a white-glove experience from start to finish. This is a dynamic role for an individual who thrives in a fast-paced environment while also being deliberate and methodical in their work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own job creation process in ATS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and schedule virtual or in-person interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Greet candidates for in-person interviews, provide a tour of the office, and ensure refreshments or lunch is provided as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accompany candidates to in-person interviews and in between interviews, wrap up in-person interviews, and see candidates out the door&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide interviewers with candidate resumes, virtual meeting links or reserved interview rooms, and other necessary items to ensure a seamless interview experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad hoc recruiting tasks and projects that align with recruiting or company goals and initiatives such as interviewer training, employer branding, referral program, candidate experience, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidate-centric and conscientious: you act as a steward of the company and put candidate experience at the center of your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and communicative: you speak and write clearly and thoughtfully with candidates and hiring teams to ensure a positive and successful experience for everyone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail: you are diligently organized, stay on top of scheduling activities, and partner with your recruiter to ensure candidates are progressing through interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth and learning mindset: you are a lifelong learner and remain curious about how your work aligns and evolves with the success and goals of the recruiting team and company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years experience in the recruitment space, preferably at a high-growth mid-stage organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to multi-task and schedule a high volume of interviews with a sense of urgency and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Greenhouse and Gem Scheduling, or other similar applicant tracking system or scheduling tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess high integrity in handling confidential and sensitive information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past experience with driving or supporting projects from conception to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in the San Francisco Bay Area and able to come into the office 4x/week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$84,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$98,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Revenue Accountant, you will be the technical backbone of Peregrine’s revenue recognition function. You will own the mechanics of ASC 606 in practice: building and maintaining the monthly revenue waterfall, preparing revenue journal entries, and drafting the workpapers that support our revenue recognition process. You’ll work closely with members of the accounting team, independently preparing technical analyses and recommendations and contributing to the continued build-out of our revenue processes and systems. This role combines disciplined monthly close execution with contract-level analysis, audit support, and system implementation work. You’ll bring strong technical grounding, curiosity, and a critical eye for detail, with the opportunity to deepen your revenue accounting expertise in a growing SaaS business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the monthly revenue waterfall calculation and maintenance end-to-end, including the underlying formulas and validation checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and post monthly revenue journal entries for U.S. and international contracts as part of the close calendar, including multi-currency transactions and related FX considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare recurring revenue trend and variance analyses and ad hoc reports, reviewing account activity to identify discrepancies, explain changes, and provide meaningful financial insights to the accounting team, including the Controller and CFO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently draft the annual ASC 606 workpaper set, including performance obligation (POB) analyses, standalone selling price (SSP) reviews, and contract-level revenue patterns, along with supporting schedules for month-end close and audit requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze contract-level performance obligations and revenue-recognition questions, preparing recommended positions for review and approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor service-delivery status and revenue-recognition triggers across the contract population, flagging timing changes before they land in close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support contract intake by partnering cross-functionally with the sales, legal, and contracts teams to triage contract-related correspondence, confirm terms, keep the contract repository current and organized, and analyze contract trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support system implementations, including contributing to design and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad hoc revenue accounting projects as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field &lt;strong&gt;or equivalent experience.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive SaaS revenue accounting experience in applying ASC 606.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of the ASC 606 five-step model, including SSP, contract modifications, variable consideration, and performance obligation identification, with the ability to independently draft technically sound workpapers, identify open judgment questions, and present clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with month-end close mechanics: journal entry preparation, account reconciliation, multi-currency transactions, and audit workpaper support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong spreadsheet skills, including formulas and reconciling data across systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to translate complex revenue information into clear analyses and collaborate effectively across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven record of accuracy and follow-through, with the ability to work against a fixed close calendar and flag risk to it in advance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt; 2+ years of public accounting experience, ideally at a Big Four firm, ideally with technology or SaaS clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt; NetSuite experience, and exposure to government or public-sector contracts such as milestone billing, multi-agency or consortium billing structures, or public-sector procurement terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &#39;Segoe UI&#39;,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$105,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot; data-reactroot=&quot;&quot;&gt;Peregrine Technologies is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We celebrate diversity and are a proud equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an engineering team, we believe strongly that empathy improves our solutions. Seeing how people use the product is a priority and the way we get to the right answer. Engineers will have the opportunity to work closely with our team onsite to understand the variety of use cases that Peregrine serves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our core engineering teams. You’ll work cross-functionally with design and product management to build systems that are robust, scalable, and user-centered. Our teams tackle a range of challenges, from enabling real-time user collaboration on detailed maps to building high-scale backend architecture for ingesting billions of data points.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value both ownership and collaboration—you will take full responsibility for major features and work closely with other engineers to drive them to completion. We believe that humility and empathy are essential for building the right solutions—you will collaborate directly with our deployment team and users as we iterate to solve their problems. Perseverance and creativity are crucial to executing our vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for strong developers to join our small but growing team. As a Senior Software Engineer, you’ll have vast ownership across our stacks, making decisions that will have an outsized impact for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll take on some of our most complex challenges—like designing scalable permission systems to manage access to terabytes of data across thousands of organizations. You’ll help build intuitive controls that let organizations decide what data to share, when to share it, and with whom. You’ll also architect frameworks for secure collaboration, enabling seamless partnerships while maintaining data sovereignty and compliance. And you’ll create advanced sharing mechanisms that strike the right balance between openness and security to unlock the full potential of cross-organizational collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our stack is constantly evolving but based on a backend foundation of Python, Django, Celery, Airflow, and Kafka; a frontend built in React, Redux, and Mapbox; data stores including PostgreSQL and Elasticsearch; machine learning models hosted in Bedrock and Sagemaker; and with AWS, Pulumi, Terraform, and Kubernetes as our underlying infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire and drive to own large portions of the application from start to finish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for crafting and shipping software solutions that delight users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive on ambiguity and love taking on hard problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent technical vision with the ability to synthesize product requests into strong and reliable software components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience working with cross-functional software development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping and iterating on production-grade software components professionally and / or in the open-source community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write robust, well tested, and well-designed code that frequently gets deployed to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of architecting and scaling distributed software systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong best practices in modern software development and comfort navigating large codebases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in San Francisco and open to working in office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
