&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Designer at Peregrine, you&#39;ll help set the design direction for how public safety teams work with data. Understanding our users is core to this role, so you&#39;ll have ample opportunities to see Peregrine in the field and bring those insights back to shape the roadmap. You&#39;ll partner with Design, Engineering, and Product leadership to define the digital renaissance of public safety and delight users who seldom get to use outstanding software, transforming complex, data-dense workflows into intuitive solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a deeply curious and inventive Staff Product Designer to lead the design of end-to-end experiences across a vast data platform. You&#39;ll move fluidly from research and problem framing to strategy to the craft and finish of every detail, and you&#39;ll raise the bar for the designers around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds exciting to you, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead our most ambitious design initiatives, from problem definition through launch, to deliver a well-executed and highly polished product that will delight users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills to influence across Design, Engineering and Business Development teams, defining scope and prioritization to ensure high-quality outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and elevate design critiques with the Design and Leadership teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with leadership to define the product strategy and craft a compelling narrative that inspires team members toward a unified outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other designers and help grow the Design discipline in a company that values exceptional user experience, including shaping our design systems, asset library, and the practices that define how we work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience* leading the design of complex software products while maintaining a relentless focus on the user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional interaction design, visual design and design thinking, with the ability to clearly articulate your thought process to peers and executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for distilling complex problems into intuitive workflows while maintaining the quality and polish of the product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to excel in a fast-moving, and sometimes unstructured environment, and to create structure where none exists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring designers and influencing beyond your immediate team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with design tools such as Figma, Sketch and Origami&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and willingness to learn and grow from a team of high-performing builders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio of design work that conveys both craft and an ability to lead and ship successful products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in the San Francisco or New York area and open to working in office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* We&#39;ve learned that people hesitate to apply without quantifiable years of experience. However, what&#39;s most important to us is the kind of experiences you&#39;ve had and the skills you&#39;ve developed along the way. Have well over 10 years of experience? That&#39;s great! Have fewer than 10 years, but feel you meet the other requirements? That&#39;s ok too! Please apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary + Benefits + Equity (if applicable) + Bonus (if applicable)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$222,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$272,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, certifications or licenses, and specific work location. Information on the benefits offered is&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://peregrine.io/careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
