&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading Silicon Valley investors, &lt;span class=&quot;discussion-id-31a93d43-caca-80de-b81c-001cca9095e7 notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Peregrine helps public safety organizations, state and local and governments, federal agencies&lt;/span&gt;, and private-sector institutions address society’s challenges with unprecedented speed and accuracy. Our AI-enabled platform turns siloed and disconnected data into operational intelligence — instantly surfacing mission-critical information to empower better, faster decisions that improve outcomes at every touchpoint. Today Peregrine supports hundreds of customers across 30+ states and two countries, serving more than 125 million people — and we’re amplifying our impact as we expand into the enterprise and internationally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to add a Staff Software Engineer, Traffic to expand our high-impact Platform team. You’ll design and build software-defined networking capabilities that enable secure, reliable, and scalable communication across Peregrine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work across cloud and Kubernetes networking, service-to-service communication, traffic management, routing, and observability—building the control planes, services, and automation that make complex networking capabilities reliable and easy to operate at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build systems that provision, manage, and scale network connectivity across customer, cloud, and Kubernetes environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build platform capabilities for service communication, routing, traffic management, segmentation, and observability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend and improve APIs and services that make networking capabilities reliable and self-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design systems for safe configuration, policy enforcement, traffic rollout, and failure recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve the reliability, scalability, and observability of networking and traffic management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead debugging of complex connectivity and traffic issues across application, Kubernetes, cloud, and network boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive architectural direction and networking standards while collaborating across Infrastructure, Security, and product engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9+ years of experience in software, infrastructure, or network engineering roles, with a focus on building and operating systems at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills (e.g., Python, Go, or similar) with experience building production systems or services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of networking fundamentals (e.g., TCP/IP, routing, DNS, load balancing, NAT, VPNs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud and Kubernetes networking, including concepts such as VPCs, routing, network policy, and service connectivity (service mesh and CNI experience, such as Istio or Cilium is a big plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating distributed systems or networking infrastructure (e.g., control planes, traffic management, gateways or proxies, automation systems)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging skills and ability to troubleshoot across application, system, and network boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive technical direction and make architectural decisions across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in and around one of our offices in SF, DC, or NYC and excited to work in-office.&lt;/li&gt;
